<title>JAPAN: Japan industrial output up prelim 4.1 pct July.</title>
<headline>Japan industrial output up prelim 4.1 pct July.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production in July increased a preliminary 4.1 percent from the previous month on a seasonally adjusted basis, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Friday.</p>
<p>MITI said in a statement that overall, industrial output was on a gradual upward trend although stock levels remained high.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the preliminary monthly figures:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted month-on-month (in pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>				   July    MONTH AGO     July INDEX</p>
<p> Output			  +4.1	-4.3	97.9</p>
<p> Shipments		     +3.3	-3.8	99.1</p>
<p> Inventories		   -1.1	-0.7	107.9</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>    Shipments ratio	  -4.0	+3.8	115.7</p>
<p>Unadjusted year-on-year (in pct):</p>
<p>				   July    MONTH AGO</p>
<p> Output			  +5.3	-1.0</p>
<p> Shipments		     +6.0	-0.5</p>
<p> Inventories		   +1.2	+2.6</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>    Shipments ratio	 -3.4	+4.3</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of MITI's forecasts for manufacturers' output: Seasonally adjusted, month-on-month (in pct):</p>
<p>		     Aug forecast  Sept forecast</p>
<p>		     -1.2	    +0.1</p>
